  q(GOV,'The IT department maintains servers and backups for patient data but does not decide how the data are used. What is its role?','Data custodian',['Data owner','Data steward','Data subject'],'A','Custodians protect and store data, while owners and stewards set rules for their use.',ZC),
  q(GOV,'Which method is appropriate for destroying old paper medical records?','Cross-cut shredding or pulping',['Placing them in regular trash','Recycling them whole','Storing them in an unlocked room'],'B','Destruction should be documented with the date, method and records destroyed.',ZC),
  q(GOV,'An organization labels data as public, internal, confidential or restricted. What is this practice?','Data classification',['Data mining','Data normalization','Data visualization'],'C','Classification determines what security controls each type of data needs.',ZC),
  q(GOV,'A hospital stores some patient information on paper and some in electronic systems. What is this called?','A hybrid record',['A personal health record','A data warehouse','A legal hold'],'D','Hybrid records need clear policies on which source is the official record.',ZC),
  q(GOV,'How does a policy differ from a procedure?','A policy states the rule; a procedure explains the steps to follow it',['They are the same','A procedure is broader than a policy','A policy lists step-by-step instructions, while a procedure states the goal'],'A','For example, a policy may require secure disposal, while the procedure explains how to shred.',ZC),
  q(GOV,'Which department traditionally manages patient records, coding and release of information in a hospital?','Health information management (HIM)',['Facilities management','Human resources','Materials management'],'B','HIM professionals ensure records are complete, accurate and protected.',ZC),
  q(SEC,'Which security tool monitors and controls network traffic based on a set of rules?','A firewall',['A data dictionary','An order set','A PACS'],'C','Firewalls help block unauthorized traffic between the hospital network and the internet.',ZC),
  q(SEC,'Which backup practice best protects data from ransomware and disasters?','Keeping copies offline or offsite',['Saving one copy on the same server','Never testing backups','Backing up once a year'],'D','Backups must be tested regularly to make sure data can actually be restored.',ZC),
  q(SEC,'Which HIPAA document tells patients how their health information may be used and what their rights are?','The Notice of Privacy Practices',['A business associate agreement','A data use agreement','A legal hold notice'],'A','Providers must give the notice at the first visit and post it in the office and online.',ZC),
  q(SEC,'Which type of record receives extra protection under HIPAA and usually requires specific patient authorization to release?','Psychotherapy notes',['Lab results','Billing records','Immunization records'],'B','These notes are kept separate from the rest of the medical record.',ZC),
  q(SEC,'Which federal office enforces the HIPAA Privacy and Security Rules?','The HHS Office for Civil Rights (OCR)',['The Food and Drug Administration (FDA)','The Federal Bureau of Investigation (FBI)','The Joint Commission'],'C','OCR investigates complaints and can impose fines for HIPAA violations.',ZC),
  q(SEC,'An EHR closes a session after several minutes without activity. What is this safeguard called?','Automatic logoff',['Single sign-on','Encryption at rest','Audit trail review'],'D','Automatic logoff protects records when users forget to sign out of shared workstations.',ZC),
  q(ETH,'An EHR vendor offers a hospital analyst an expensive gift during contract talks. What is the ethical concern?','A conflict of interest',['Data provenance','Alert fatigue','Data lineage'],'A','Accepting gifts can bias decisions, so most organizations have gift policies.',ZC),
  q(ETH,'Which professional code guides health information professionals on privacy, integrity and honesty?','The AHIMA Code of Ethics',['The Hippocratic Oath only','The HL7 standard','The ICD-10-CM guidelines'],'B','The AHIMA code includes protecting confidential information and refusing to falsify data.',ZC),
  q(RES,'Researchers interview patients in depth about their experience using a patient portal. What type of research is this?','Qualitative research',['Quantitative research','A meta-analysis','A randomized controlled trial'],'C','Qualitative research explores experiences and meanings through words rather than numbers.',WH),
  q(RES,'Researchers divide patients into age groups and randomly select a set number from each group. What sampling method is this?','Stratified random sampling',['Convenience sampling','Simple random sampling','Snowball sampling'],'D','Stratification makes sure each subgroup is fairly represented in the sample.',WH),
  q(RES,'In a drug trial, the control group receives a pill that looks the same but has no active ingredient. What is this pill called?','A placebo',['A confounder','A covariate','An independent variable'],'A','Placebos help separate the true drug effect from patients’ expectations.',WH),
  q(RES,'Before a large study, researchers test their survey and methods on a small group. What is this called?','A pilot study',['A meta-analysis','A case report','A cohort study'],'B','Pilot studies find problems early, before time and money are spent on the full study.',WH),
  q(RES,'A survey gives the same results when repeated under the same conditions. Which property does it have?','Reliability',['Validity','Bias','Power'],'C','A tool can be reliable without being valid if it consistently measures the wrong thing.',WH),
  q(RES,'Before designing a study, a researcher reads and summarizes what earlier studies have found. What is this?','A literature review',['A pilot study','A data audit','A meta-analysis that pools data'],'D','A literature review shows gaps in knowledge and helps shape the research question.',WH),
  q(EMER,'Software bots automatically complete repetitive tasks, such as checking insurance eligibility. What technology is this?','Robotic process automation (RPA)',['Blockchain record keeping','Virtual reality training','Ambient clinical voice recording'],'A','RPA follows set rules and frees staff from routine data entry.',ZC),
  q(EMER,'Using a patient’s genetic information in the EHR to choose the best drug and dose is part of which approach?','Precision medicine',['Telehealth','Ambient documentation','Alert fatigue'],'B','Pharmacogenomic alerts can warn clinicians when a gene affects how a drug works.',ZC)
